{"type": "root", "attrs": {"type": "node", "context": "sop", "internal": "voronoisplit", "icon": "SOP/voronoisplit", "version": "2.0", "since": "21.5", "tags": "subdivide, split", "namespace": null}, "body": [{"level": 0, "type": "title", "indent": 0, "text": ["Voronoi Split"], "extent": [144, 162]}, {"type": "summary", "indent": 0, "text": ["Cuts the geometry into small pieces according to a set of cuts defined by polylines."], "extent": [162, 255]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["Voronoi Split cuts geometry according to a set of polylines. Each line describes a cut along its mid-point.\nLines are best created with the ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/sop/voronoiadjacency", "type": "link", "text": ["Voronoi Adjacency SOP"], "fullpath": "/nodes/sop/voronoiadjacency.html"}, "."], "extent": [255, 447]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["This is a utility SOP which is similar to the ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/sop/voronoifracture", "type": "link", "text": ["Voronoi Fracture SOP"], "fullpath": "/nodes/sop/voronoifracture.html"}, ", but without any of the extra features. ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/sop/voronoifracture", "type": "link", "text": ["Voronoi Fracture"], "fullpath": "/nodes/sop/voronoifracture.html"}, " should typically be used instead of Voronoi Split."], "extent": [447, 677]}, {"level": 1, "id": "parameters", "container": true, "type": "parameters_section", "indent": 0, "role": "section", "extent": [677, 689], "body": [{"type": "parameters_item_group", "body": [{"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["Group"], "extent": [689, 697], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Subset of the input geometry to split."], "extent": [712, 764]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "group"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["Clip Points Group"], "extent": [764, 783], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Lines leaving these points will be used as clipping lines. Each point will correspond to a new piece."], "extent": [803, 914]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "clipptsgrp"}, "role": "item"}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Cut"], "extent": [914, 924], "body": [{"type": "parameters_item_group", "body": [{"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["Create Interior Surfaces"], "extent": [924, 951], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Creates faces on the interior of the geometry when performing the cutting.\n    This should typically be turned off when fracturing open surfaces, or to create a thin shell from a solid object."], "extent": [983, 1185]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "createinteriorsurfaces"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["Snapping Tolerance"], "extent": [1185, 1205], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Maximum distance to move points onto the clipping planes."], "extent": [1222, 1289]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "snaptol"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["Offset"], "extent": [1289, 1297], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Instead of cutting at the mid-point, it is offset by this distance along the line."], "extent": [1313, 1405]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "offset"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["Weight Attribute"], "extent": [1405, 1423], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["When turned on, the specified float attribute provides a ", {"type": "q", "text": ["weight"]}, " for each point, which affects where cutting planes are placed, according to the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Method"]}, "."], "extent": [1445, 1612]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "weightattrib"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["Method"], "extent": [1612, 1620], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Specifies how the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Weight Attribute"]}, " is used to place the cutting planes."], "extent": [1642, 1727]}, {"type": "dt_group", "body": [{"type": "dt", "indent": 4, "text": ["Power Distance"], "extent": [1727, 1747], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["The weight will be interpreted as the radius of a sphere centered at the point.\n        The cutting plane will be placed at the point where the ", {"scheme": "Wp", "value": "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Power_of_a_point", "type": "link", "text": ["power with respect to both spheres"], "exists": true}, " is the same. This produces a ", {"scheme": "Wp", "value": "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Power_diagram", "type": "link", "text": ["power diagram"], "exists": true}, ". If the radii are equal, this results in a normal Voronoi diagram."], "extent": [1747, 2094]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 4, "text": ["Ratio"], "extent": [2094, 2105], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["The cutting plane for each connected pair of points will be placed such that the ratio of the distances from each point will be the same as the ratio of the weights. \n        The plane will be closer to points with smaller weight and farther from points with larger weight."], "extent": [2105, 2401]}], "container": true}], "container": true}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "weightmethod"}, "role": "item"}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Output Attributes"], "extent": [2401, 2425], "body": [{"type": "parameters_item_group", "body": [{"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["Primitive Cell Point"], "extent": [2425, 2448], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["When turned on, creates a primitive attribute storing the point from the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Clip Polylines"]}, " geometry, which corresponds to the fractured piece.\n    This can be used to build unique names to identify each piece."], "extent": [2470, 2690]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "cellptattrib"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["Primitive Clip Point"], "extent": [2690, 2712], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["When turned on, creates a primitive attribute on the interior surface primitives that stores the point number of the adjacent cell point at that surface.\n    This parameter is only available when ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Create Interior Surfaces"]}, " is enabled. It can be used to identify adjacent pieces that should be connected by constraints in a simulation."], "extent": [2734, 3076]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "clipptattrib"}, "role": "item"}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}]}], "text": "Parameters"}, {"level": 1, "id": "inputs", "container": true, "type": "inputs_section", "indent": 0, "role": "section", "extent": [3076, 3084], "body": [{"type": "dt_group", "body": [{"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["Geometry to Split"], "extent": [3084, 3104], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The geometry to cut."], "extent": [3104, 3130]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["Clip Polylines"], "extent": [3130, 3146], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["A set of polylines which define how the geometry will be cut."], "extent": [3146, 3217]}], "container": true}], "container": true}], "text": "Inputs"}, {"level": 1, "id": "related", "container": true, "type": "related_section", "indent": 0, "role": "section", "extent": [3217, 3226], "body": [{"type": "bullet_group", "body": [{"blevel": 2, "type": "bullet", "indent": 0, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/sop/voronoiadjacency", "type": "link", "text": "", "fullpath": "/nodes/sop/voronoiadjacency.html"}], "extent": [3226, 3256]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "bullet", "indent": 0, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/sop/voronoifracture", "type": "link", "text": "", "fullpath": "/nodes/sop/voronoifracture.html"}], "extent": [3256, 3285]}], "container": true}], "text": "Related"}], "title": ["Voronoi Split"], "summary": ["Cuts the geometry into small pieces according to a set of cuts defined by polylines."]}